Keystone Privacy Policy

Effective Date: 04/09/2026

1. Overview

Keystone (“we”, “our”, or “us”) provides a Jira-integrated application designed to help teams understand sprint capacity, workload, and delivery risk.

This Privacy Policy explains what data we access, how we use it, and how it is handled.

2. Data We Access

Keystone operates within Atlassian’s Forge platform and accesses data through Jira APIs. 

We may access the following types of data:

Jira issues (including summaries, descriptions, fields, and status)
Sprint and board data
User account identifiers (such as accountId)
Project and team configuration data
We may also persist certain data within Atlassian Forge storage, including user identifiers (such as accountId), configuration data, and application-generated content required for app functionality.

3. How We Use Data

We use this data solely to provide the functionality of the Keystone application, including:

Calculating sprint health metrics
Evaluating capacity vs workload
Identifying at-risk work
Displaying meeting and timeline impacts
Supporting configuration settings defined by administrators

We do not use this data for advertising, profiling, or marketing purposes.

4. Data Storage

Keystone is built on Atlassian Forge.

- Data is stored using Atlassian-hosted infrastructure (Forge storage)
- This may include Atlassian account identifiers (such as accountId), user configuration data, and application-generated content
- We do not store customer data on external servers
- We do not transfer data outside Atlassian infrastructure

Keystone may store the following data within Atlassian-hosted Forge storage:

- Atlassian account identifiers (such as accountId)
- User configuration and preferences
- Team and administrative configuration records
- Application-generated content such as meeting notes, summaries, or feed items

This data is stored solely to support app functionality and is not used for advertising or external processing.

5. Data Sharing

We do not sell, rent, or share customer data with third parties.

Data is only processed within the Atlassian platform to deliver app functionality.

6. Data Retention

Keystone retains data only as long as necessary to support app functionality.

Data stored via Forge storage is retained while the app is installed
When the app is uninstalled, associated stored data is removed in accordance with Atlassian’s platform behavior
7. Security

Keystone relies on Atlassian Forge security and infrastructure.

Authentication is handled by Atlassian
No user credentials are stored by Keystone
All API access is authorized through Atlassian
8. Third-Party Services

Keystone does not require:

External accounts
Third-party integrations
External data processors
9. Data Roles and Responsibilities

Keystone acts as a data processor on behalf of the customer.

The customer (the Atlassian site administrator or organization) is the data controller and is responsible for managing user data and permissions within Jira.

10. User Rights

As Keystone processes data within Jira, data access and control are governed by:

Atlassian account permissions
Jira project permissions
Organization-level controls

Users should contact their Jira administrator for requests related to access, correction, or deletion of data.

11. Changes to This Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time.

Updates will be reflected with a revised effective date.

